  "note": "Speculative (Step 7, derivation A): p.80 prints no lamp, relay or indicator state for any step, so every expect is derived from the wiring and the p.80 rule that the number on the slide switches (RIGHT = 0, LEFT = 1) is displayed in the binary output lights. Wires = as_printed = programs.json wiresEffective (67, no erratum on any wire). Script: power on, all switches RIGHT (000000); enter the three-bit number 101 on switches 4, 5, 6 (000101); three left shifts done in the p.80 order (switch 1 takes switch 2's position ... switch 5 takes switch 6's, switch 6 to zero; multiply by 8: 001010, 010100, 101000); three right shifts in the p.80 order (switch 6 takes switch 5's ... switch 2 takes switch 1's, switch 1 to zero) back to 000101; a fourth right shift drops the low 1 off switch 6 (000010, the remainder is lost); then all six LEFT (111111, the accumulator limit, no overflow because no pushbutton is held). A settle follows every switch move and a 1 s advance precedes each expect so a lamp that just went out is no longer dim. Derivation: with pushbuttons 4-6 released each relay-adder carry is 0, so lamp n = switch n; relay 4 operates exactly when switch 5 is LEFT (4F/5S, 5R/6T, 6N-6L via relay 6 N.C., 6L/6Z, pushbutton 6 N.C. to +); relays 1, 2, 3 and 5 stay released; relay 6's coil is open (6F unwired) and indicator 4 is unwired (4C), so both stay dark; indicator 6 is the overflow lamp (1V-1U-M10-6C-6E-) and needs a carry into stage 1.",
